\ A raise reached through a tail-position `when`. The interpreter tail-calls `when` and pops its
\ frame, so the chain carries no combinator row. That chain is the target every tier converges on.
\
\ `boom` declares its effect, so under eager both words compile. The compiled `go` reaches `when`
\ through its fallback boundary, and the `if` inside `when` hands `boom` back as a tail call, so
\ the compiled `boom` raises after the `if` frame is gone. Both runs check this file against one
\ golden. The AOT suite builds it through `.source` redirects with their own goldens.

boom: ( -- ) [ f "kaboom" EUserThrown make-error throw ] ;
go: ( ? -- ) [ [ boom ] when ] ;

[ t go ] [ inspect print-line ] recover
